aplay: map the Bluetooth volume linearly onto the mixer's range

bluealsa-aplay converts the volume a phone sends (0-127) to a mixer level with a
loudness formula: every halving of the phone's volume lowers the mixer by 10 dB.
On a USB DAC that leaves the output within 10 dB of full scale for the whole upper
half of the phone's slider, much louder than the same slider position on a computer.

Use the mixer's own scale instead, in both directions: 40% on the phone is 40% of
the mixer range, as "amixer set PCM 40%" would set it.

Upstream: not submitted; a change of behaviour that this project wants.

